winemac: Do not swap native buffers for a front-buffer flush.

Follow up the b5ab3b15 backport. win32u_wgl_context_flush has already
executed the caller's glFlush/glFinish before notifying the drawable.
macdrv_flush_opengl_context calls NSOpenGLContext.flushBuffer, which also
swaps a double-buffered drawable. GL_FLUSH_PRESENT alone is not a swap
request (it is also sent while binding a context). For emulated front
buffers, win32u separately invokes the swap callback for GL_FLUSH_FORCE_SWAP.

Keep client_surface_present and A6 synchronization, but leave native buffer
exchange to macdrv_surface_swap. Removing just this call restores BlueCG HD
mode 1 loading/login on OpenGL, with both A6 and the rest of PR #2 retained.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -2023,11 +2023,9 @@
     if (flags & GL_FLUSH_INTERVAL) set_swap_interval(context, base->interval);
     if ((flags & GL_FLUSH_UPDATED) || macdrv_opengl_context_backing_sync_pending(context->context))
         make_context_current(context, context->read_view == client->cocoa_view);
-    if (flags & GL_FLUSH_PRESENT)
-    {
-        macdrv_flush_opengl_context(context->context);
-        client_surface_present(base->client);
-    }
+    /* GL_FLUSH_PRESENT is not a buffer-swap request. win32u has already
+     * flushed GL commands; GL_FLUSH_FORCE_SWAP uses the swap callback. */
+    if (flags & GL_FLUSH_PRESENT) client_surface_present(base->client);
 }
 
 
